{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"Fixed the `HTTPResponse` streaming decoder defects using only the standard library. Bounded reads now handle gzip member boundaries and flush raw and chained deflate at EOF. Repeated cached reads preserve `self._body`. Invalid decode-mode switches raise before consuming data, and `read(0, decode_content=False)` returns `b\"\"`.\n\n**Release remains blocked.** The default Python 3.9 failed during import, so I reran `python3 benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/run_checks.py` with Python 3.15.0 first on `PATH`. It ran all four checks and exited with status `1` (`FAILED (failures=1)`).\n\n| Check | Final result |\n|---|---|\n| `test_gzip_multi_member_bounded_read` | PASS |\n| `test_optional_brotli_and_zstd_codecs_available` | FAIL |\n| `test_raw_deflate_eof_flush_streaming` | PASS |\n| `test_reject_decode_toggle_before_consuming` | PASS |\n\nSupplemental checks passed for bounded `read`, `read1`, ordinary and chunked `stream`, cache preservation, and resuming decoded reads after a rejected switch.\n\n### Blockers & Flaws\n\nThe codec availability gate failed because neither `brotli` nor `brotlicffi` is installed in the Python 3.15 environment. I independently confirmed that its Zstandard backend is available."}}
